like our friendly neighborhood  spider-man developer insomniac games has  rarely taken itself too seriously  it's protagonists range from talking  dragons to gun-toting lombaxes to punk  rock sanitation workers but also like  spider-man there is a wealth of ability  creativity and wisdom beneath that  playful veneer throughout the years  insomniac has bounced between 3d  platformers third-person action games  first-person shooters and open-world  playgrounds its portfolio is as colorful  as it is diverse yet in the grand scheme  of things the studio's expertise has  gone largely underappreciated insomniac  s-- 1998 breakout hits spyro sold almost  5 million copies the first retching  clank also sold well in 2002 breaking  3.5 million in sales and establishing a  new IP as the years rolled by however  the company's sales continually dropped  off now the games performed poorly by  any means but insomniac struggled to  regain the clout it had earned on the  ps1 the studio explored a darker tone  with 2006's resistance fall of man but  as was the case with ratchet the  franchise sold fewer copies with each  new release by the time insomniac  launched resistance 3 and it's decent  co-op shooter fuse we had already seen  ps3 standouts such as mgs for God of War  3 Gran Turismo 5 and the blockbuster  Uncharted Saga that's not to mention  third-party games such as call of duty  or grand theft auto  although insomniac played a crucial role  in the ps3s lifespan it's since taken a  historical backseat to the juggernauts  of its time  then came the newest console generation  and in 2014 the first insomniac title  made exclusively for a Microsoft  platform sunset overdrive is colorful  and abrasive it's on ashamed of its  goofy overtones it's also an insomniac  game in every sense with thrilling  platforming inventive weapons and a  refusal to take itself seriously it was  a critical darling and in my humble  opinion one of the best games on Xbox  one but this was a new IP early in a  console generation on a platform whose  sales had yet to gain momentum  despite sunset OverDrive's high purchase  rate for Xbox one owners it was no  commercial hit four years later it's  hailed as a  halt classic and in those intervening  four years insomniac games would double  down on its mantra of constant evolution  it experimented with VR creating a  competitive spell casting game a 3d  brawler and the fantastic horror title  edge of nowhere the studio also teamed  up with retailer Game Stop on song of  the deep a Metroidvania that doubled as  an outreach effort to gain stops  customers insomniac even branched into  cinema in 2016 it released the Ratchet  and Clank film to coincide with a  Ratchet and Clank remake on ps4 the  latter marked the company's first outing  on Sony's current console and a chance  to learn the ps4 s architecture for the  game it had planned next  throughout its history insomniac games  has been no stranger to success it's  been a staple of Sony's catalogues since  1998 it released one of the Xbox ones  most beloved titles to date its games  have frequently sold in the millions and  aside from several middling releases  found almost universal acclaim and  through it all the studio has managed to  remain independent but in a conversation  about respected triple-a developers  insomniac is often overshadowed by the  likes of Rockstar Naughty Dog Blizzard  Nintendo or say they project red  a few months ago insomniac CEO Ted Price  told the LA Times that the studio has  always seen themselves as somewhat of an  underdog and in a recent chat creative  director Brian in Tahar told me the same  thing so I guess it's fitting that  insomniac games is finally getting the  spotlight it deserves with one of pop  culture's most famous underdogs Peter  Parker the superhero toiling beneath a  mask for a city that often takes him for  granted a few years ago you might  remember the rumor circulating about the  next spider-man game according to 